In article <1991Mar2.123022.10348@doe.utoronto.ca> david@doe.utoronto.ca (David Megginson) writes:
>Here are some suggestions for limiting the power of the ring of conflict:
>
>1) Have it affect only monsters who respect Elbereth (ie., not @).
>
>2) Have it use up much more food than even the ring of regeneration, so that
>   anyone wearing it has to eat every 3 or 4 rounds.
etc.

I disagree with this. A ring of conflict is very powerfull for a beginner but
you can't win a game with it. When you limit the power of the ring of conflict
you remove a nice "weapon" from the game. Why is a Mjollnir (much more
powerfull) alowed and a ring of conflict not? The ring of conflict can be
especially used against hill orcs and Uruk-hai's but fails against mumakils,
jellys and minotaurs. For opulent thrones, treasure zoos and baraks there
are other tricks like stealth (from an elven cloak par example).

The ring of conflict has already a great disadvantage, you don't get experience
points. So, if you use the ring without cease then maybe you can reach dungeon
level 20, but then you have serious problem.

The power of the ring is overestimated by beginners!

